From 46be47caadbc743a6fbf10fdb03138b139a6a9b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <andrewyoull86@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] core: yuv420p brightness; NEON loops for mixes and
 overlays

brightness works on yuv420p as it is (luma towards black, chroma towards
grey) instead of converting to yuv422 and back.

core_neon.c has NEON versions of the dissolve's mix, brightness's scale
and composite's yuv420p blends, built with -mfpu=neon on 32-bit ARM
only. They run only when the application sets MLT_NEON=1 in MLT's
environment (the CPU has NEON); otherwise the C loops run. 8.8 fixed
point: a result can differ by one from the C.

composite passes consumer.fast_scale on to the b frame.
---
